# WebVeld Licensing

The WebVeld project uses a dual-licensing model to distinguish between specification text and software/tooling:

- **Specification and Documentation:** Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY 4.0) — full text under "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International" below, and at <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>.
- **Software, Tooling, and Examples:** MIT License — full text under "MIT License" below, and at <https://opensource.org/license/mit>.

---

## Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International

All specification text and documentation within the `doc/` directory, including [`doc/webveld-spec.md`](doc/webveld-spec.md), [`doc/webveld-motivation.md`](doc/webveld-motivation.md), [`doc/webveld-roadmap.md`](doc/webveld-roadmap.md), and related architectural documents, are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0) License.

You are free to:
- **Share** — copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format.
- **Adapt** — remix, transform, and build upon the material for any purpose, even commercially.

Under the following terms:
- **Attribution** — You must give appropriate credit, provide a link to the license, and indicate if changes were made. You may do so in any reasonable manner, but not in any way that suggests the licensor endorses you or your use.
- **No additional restrictions** — You may not apply legal terms or technological measures that legally restrict others from doing anything the license permits.

For the full legal text of the CC-BY 4.0 license, visit:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

